<title>USA: Integra artificial skin approved in France.</title>
<headline>Integra artificial skin approved in France.</headline>
<dateline>PLAINSBORO, N.J. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integra LifeSciences Corp on Monday said it received full and final approval to sell Integra Artificial Skin in France for the treatment of burns and for reconstructive surgery.</p>
<p>France had previously received special permission for surgeons to use the product to treat burn victims on an emergency basis, Integra said.</p>
<p>So far, 20 French surgeons have already been trained to use the artificial skin, and the company is continuing its training programs, it said.</p>
